# `xscaleinten` Rung-3 Witness, Repair, and Kill Table on `-E iq80321`

## 1. Executive Summary & Defect Disposition

The defect in [cpu_arm_coproc.c](file:///C:/DocumentNoSnc/CC/GXEMUL/GXEMUL-SEC/src/cpus/cpu_arm_coproc.c#L310-L316) (`arm_coproc_i80321_6()`, `crm == 0`, `crn == 0`) terminates the emulator on any guest read of the Intel 80321 `INTEN` (Interrupt Enable) register via Coprocessor 6 (`MRC p6, 0, Rd, c0, c0, 0`):

```c
		case 0:	if (l_bit) {
				cpu->cd.arm.r[rd] = cpu->cd.arm.i80321_inten;
				fatal("TODO: XScale read from inten?\n");
				exit(1);
			} else
				cpu->cd.arm.i80321_inten = cpu->cd.arm.r[rd];
			break;
```

In GXemul's architecture, `dev_i80321.c:446` explicitly wires this register into the interrupt controller via pointer aliasing:
```c
d->enable = &cpu->cd.arm.i80321_inten;
```
Both the backing store and interrupt gating semantics (`*d->status & *d->enable` in `i80321_assert()`) were fully implemented; the read arm correctly transferred the register value to `cpu->cd.arm.r[rd]` before needlessly aborting.

**Repair Applied**: Deletion of the two terminating lines (`fatal(...)` and `exit(1);`), preserving the register assignment without emitting any false "unimplemented" diagnostic.

---

## 2. Measurement Verification: Pre-Fix vs. Post-Fix

Measurements were performed on the IQ80321 platform (`-E iq80321`) using a 7-arm guest assembly harness loaded at PA/VA `0x00008000` (strictly above the `0x4000-0x7FFF` L1 translation table).

### Summary of Results (26 Assertions)

| Arm / Assertion Focus | Pre-Fix (`witness_committed.out`) | Post-Fix (`witness_fix.out`) | Status |
| :--- | :--- | :--- | :--- |
| **D (Data Transfer & Reset)** | 1 / 9 passed (`D_P2_POISON` passed; `D_TODO_ABS`, `D_SURVIVE`, `D_RESET`, `D_S1`, `D_ZERO`, `D_S2`, `D_OP2`, `D_MARKER` failed) | **9 / 9 passed** | **Repaired** |
| **LNC (Latent Non-Canonical)** | 2 / 5 passed (`LNC_P2`, `LNC_COND` passed; `LNC_TODO_ABS`, `LNC_SUB`, `LNC_MARKER` failed) | **5 / 5 passed** | **Repaired** |
| **E (Exception Refusal)** | 1 / 1 passed (opcode1 != 0 dies with exit 1) | **1 / 1 passed** (still dies) | Preserved |
| **S (Sibling Parity)** | 2 / 2 passed (unimplemented write arms die) | **2 / 2 passed** (still die) | Preserved |
| **RD15 (Rd == 15 PC Transfer)**| 1 / 2 passed (`RD15_P2` passed; `RD15_SURVIVE` failed) | **2 / 2 passed** | **Repaired** |
| **ANCHOR (Side-Effect Gating)**| 1 / 4 passed (`ANCHOR_P2` passed; `ANCHOR_M1`, `ANCHOR_EXC`, `ANCHOR_CONTRAST` failed) | **4 / 4 passed** | **Repaired** |
| **CONTRACT (X4, A2, D_TRR0)** | 3 / 3 passed (`X4_NOP`, `A2_INSTALLED`, `D_TRR0` pass) | **3 / 3 passed** | Preserved |
| **TOTAL** | **11 / 26 passed** (15 failing) | **26 / 26 passed** (0 failing) | **100% Repaired** |

### Key Guard & Contract Checks
- **P2 Vacuity Guard**: Verified that every destination register holds its distinct poison value (`0xDEADBEEF`, `0xBAADF00D`, etc.) immediately prior to its read instruction.
- **X4 Contract**: NOP destination verification confirmed that `mov r0, r0` leaves `r0` poisoned and does not acquire `S1`.
- **A2 Contract**: Confirmed complete absence of the generic `arm_mcr_mrc: uninstalled coproc 6` diagnostic.
- **Diagnostic Absence**: Verified that `fatal: TODO: XScale read from inten?` is present under pre-fix and completely absent post-fix.

---

